      "category": "common_knowledge",
      "summary": "When an OAuth token refresh endpoint returns 429, retry with bounded exponential backoff: up to four attempts, starting at one second and doubling, with full jitter. Do not retry beyond the fourth attempt; treat the last 429 as a hard failure and surface it. Retrying without jitter causes thundering herd behavior where throttled clients synchronize and remain throttled. Continuing to retry without a bound converts one rate-limited endpoint into an outage for all callers.",
